    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Weathering is strictly an in-situ (static) process, whereas erosion involves transportation (dynamic).",
        "Cirques, Aretes, and U-shaped valleys are glacial erosional landforms, while Moraines are glacial depositional features.",
        "Mushroom rocks and Yardangs are created by wind erosion; Loess and Seif dunes are wind deposition landforms."
